  "funFact": "Peanut worms (sipunculans) were classified as their own phylum for over a century, but modern genomics placed them firmly within Annelida — the same phylum as earthworms and lugworms. Despite both being soft marine 'worms', a peanut worm is closer to an earthworm than to a ribbon worm — ribbon worms (nemerteans) belong to an entirely different phylum.",
